  "_about_request_rules": "Request shapes a model refuses, from Anthropic's model reference (as of 2026-10-01), applied by zylch/llm/roles/request_rules.py at the client boundary after the budget reservation: keys are model-id prefixes in both forms (direct and OpenRouter catalogue id), the longest prefix wins. sampling: 'drop' removes temperature/top_p/top_k (Opus 4.7 and later, Sonnet 5), 'drop_non_default' only a non-default value (Sonnet 5.5; its OpenRouter id drops all, as Sonnet endpoints refuse sampling under require_parameters); forced_tool_choice 'auto' downgrades tool_choice any/tool (Fable 5.1, Opus 5.5, Sonnet 5.5); thinking_off is what turns default thinking off (Sonnet 5 and Opus 5 think when thinking is omitted; Sonnet 5.5 takes between_tools, not disabled; Opus 5.5 cannot, null). Rules only remove or relax fields, so the reserved bound still holds. The resolver ignores this key.",
